WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:01.767
-Our first guest tonight is

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.367
an Emmy-nominated comedian

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:06.033
you know from her work
on "Saturday Night Live"

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:07.767
and in movies
such as "Ghostbusters"

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:08.834
and "Coming to America."

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:10.868
You can see her
in the new comedy series

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:14.234
"Our Flag Means Death,"
which is streaming on HBO Max,

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:15.467
with new episodes
every Thursday.

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:16.701
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:19.601
our very good friend
Leslie Jones, everybody!

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:20.701
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:21.901
-Hey!
-There she is.

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:24.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:27.501
-What's up, baby?
-Leslie.

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:29.934
I have thought about you
so often this year.

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:31.834
You are one of the people
that I most associate

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:33.567
with the Los Angeles Rams.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:35.801
You're such a giant fan
of the team

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:39.501
and I was so happy for you
when they won the Super Bowl.

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:41.701
Are you still on cloud nine?

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:43.033
-I'm a new fan.

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:45.868
Like it's easy to become a fan
when they win it,

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:46.634
you know what I'm saying?

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:48.133
So, when I got to L.A.,

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:50.634
I was like,
"Oh, Odell Beckham's on that?

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:53.033
Oh, Von Miller? Okay,
I'mma start cheering for them."

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:55.133
And, as soon as I started
cheering for them,

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:56.400
that's when
they started winning.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.834
That's what I'mma tell myself.

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.400
-You know what?
This is very noble

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:02.467
because a lot of new fans
won't admit to everybody

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.167
that they came to it late
in the game,

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:06.634
but I think that's very,
very strong of you.

00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:08.567
Very strong character to admit.
-You know I'm strong.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:09.868
I'm strong, though.

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:12.467
I'm strong and a strong
character, so, yeah.

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:15.300
-But I hope people will
forgive me for thinking

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.834
You've been a lifelong Rams fan.

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:19.601
I just want to show one
of your many Instagram videos.

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.167
This is when the Rams were going
to the Super Bowl.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:23.133
This does not strike me
as someone who's a new fan.

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:24.267
Let's take a look.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:25.667
Aaaaah!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:27.367
Aaaaaaah!

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:30.133
I thought they was gonna
[bleep] choke!

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:31.334
[ Laughter ]
They didn't choke!

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:33.968
[Bleep] [Bleep] [Bleep]

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.667
[ Laughter ]
Aaaaaaaaah!

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:37.767
We going to the Super Bowl,
bitch!

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:39.100
We going!

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.534
-So, I mean, I think there are
a lot of people

00:01:42.534 --> 00:01:44.000
who've been lifelong fans
who were like,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.834
"Man, I don't care about them
as much as her."

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:46.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:48.534
-Because, see, I knew the Rams

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:50.567
when Eric Dickerson was playing
with them, so.

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:52.000
-Sure.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.033
That's the real deal.

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:54.767
Look, it all counts.

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:55.634
So, listen,

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:56.868
you had a cool thing happen,

00:01:56.868 --> 00:01:58.334
which is not only was your team
in the Super Bowl

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.868
and not only did they win,
you also had a Super Bowl ad

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:02.501
with some other
famous Joneses --

00:02:02.501 --> 00:02:04.534
Rashida Jones,
Tommy Lee Jones.

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:09.100
Was it a lifelong goal
to do a Super Bowl ad?

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.801
-Y'all love to put
lifelong things on.

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:13.801
-Were you on cloud nine, Leslie?

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:17.267
[ Laughter ]
-It's a Super Bowl
commercial, man!

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:19.000
I mean, yeah, it was fun.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.367
It was very fun to do because,
you know, I love Tommy Lee,

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:24.200
even though we wasn't on set
at the same time.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.534
People think we was like

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:27.200
really driving the trucks
and everything.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.901
No, we was on the set on top
of these roller things

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:32.934
inside of the truck, acting like
we was driving the trucks.

00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:34.234
Was I supposed to tell that,
Seth?

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:35.901
-I don't know.
I just like that I'm like,

00:02:35.901 --> 00:02:38.200
"Was it a dream come true?"
And you're like, "No, and also,

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.400
we didn't even meet each other."

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:45.234
-But, when he got on set --
-Again, I love --

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:49.234
The honesty, as always,
is just your main export.

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:51.100
They said that, when he got
on set, he was like --

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.267
[ As Tommy Lee Jones ]
I want to know two things --
what am I driving

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:54.634
and where's Leslie Jones?

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:57.701
[ Laughter ]
So that happened.
-That's pretty good.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:03:00.133
I'm thinking right there,
we can step back and say

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:02.534
it was an accomplishment.

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:05.667
Hey, you also talk a lot,
and I think all of us enjoy,

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:07.234
every time there's an Olympics,

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:09.701
you sort of regale us
with your videos.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:10.968
Winter Olympics --

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:13.367
are you a fan
of the Winter Olympics sports?

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:14.868
Is there any part of you
that wishes

00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:17.267
you had taken them up
as a young person?

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:18.501
-No.
-Okay.

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:20.467
[ Laughter ]
No.

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:22.100
I mean,
I love the Winter Olympics

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:25.634
because I love the Olympics,
but none of that, none of that.

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:28.767
I don't wish to jump
off a mountain of snow.

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:31.000
I don't wish to go down a hill,

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.901
especially with that tree
out there murdering everybody.

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:37.434
[ Laughter ]
I don't wish to get
into a go-cart on sled,

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:39.100
like a sled cart.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.234
[ Laughter ]
No, I don't wish
to do none of that.

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:44.701
[ Laughter ]
But I do wish to watch them.

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:46.133
Especially when they crash.
-What about the luge?

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:47.634
Is the luge what you mean,
or is that --

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:51.133
What about the luge?
-Luge, buge, cuge, all that.

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:52.968
[ Laughter ]
I'm not doing none of it.

00:03:52.968 --> 00:03:56.300
It involves blades and a tunnel.
No, thank you.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:59.300
[ Laughter ]
-So that means hockey's out.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.968
-Yes! Especially because you'll
get your fingers cut off

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:04.334
[ Laughter ]
and then the puck
just flying everywhere.

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:07.100
Do you see hockey players
never have no teeth?

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.567
[ Laughter ]
No. No. No, sir.
-You have beautiful teeth.

00:04:09.567 --> 00:04:11.400
You wouldn't want
to lose your teeth.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.601
-Man, I have beautiful teeth.
-I'm taking my kids skiing

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:15.467
right now.
I'm teaching them how to ski.

00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:17.067
Would you ever want to come out?
-Of course you are.

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:18.567
Of course you are, white person.

00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:20.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:21.767
-Yeah, it's their birthright.

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:22.901
It's their birthright.
-Yeah.

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:24.968
I mean, like I wouldn't
even understand

00:04:24.968 --> 00:04:26.968
a white person
that has never been skiing.

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:28.300
I wouldn't even understand it.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.868 --> 00:04:32.133
Only time I've been on ski trips
is to do comedy

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:35.367
and I sit by the fire
in the ski boots.

00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:37.601
I don't, no.

00:04:37.601 --> 00:04:39.567
-You were an athlete
growing up, right?

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:42.734
You were a very talented
basketball player.

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:44.367
-Ah, I mean,
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:45.501
I was good when I wanted to be.

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:47.968
I was very inconsistent.
-Okay.

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:49.934
-But when I wanted
to be good, I was good.
-What would you attribute

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:53.467
your inconsistency to?

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:54.701
-Just, you know,

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:56.334
not really loving basketball

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:57.701
as much as everybody
thought I could.

00:04:57.701 --> 00:05:01.501
I was tall and I could make
a lay-up and, yeah, no.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.033
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:07.133
And so was there a moment --
When you first did comedy,

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:10.033
did the light go on and you
realized, "Oh, this is it"?

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:12.968
-Dude, as soon as I touched
the mic,

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:17.033
as soon as I touched the mic,
it felt like home.

00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:19.501
I felt like I had been doing it
for years.

00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:21.601
So I was like, "Oh!

00:05:21.601 --> 00:05:23.501
I'm doing this
for the rest of my life.

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:25.033
Oh, this is so easy."

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.367
Like yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:28.234
-Well, you certainly make it
look easy as well.

00:05:28.234 --> 00:05:29.834
We're going to come back
and have a bunch of questions

00:05:29.834 --> 00:05:31.334
about your new show.
We'll be right back

00:05:31.334 --> 00:05:33.133
[ Cheering and applause ]
with more from Leslie Jones.

